 "strength": 5, "prov": "verified", "layer": "public", "note": "This is a repeatable working pattern, not a one-off: you use coursework as a first draft of publishable work. It is also the clearest evidence that you can carry an idea across registers, which is the translator claim in a form you can date.", "type": "Evidence"}, {"id": "ev:mlp_research_design", "label": "Designed a study of energy justice across a national sociotechnical regime", "detail": "Using Geels' multi-level perspective, mapped keystone actors across an innovation ecosystem (ASU, DOE, ISRO), industry (GE, PG&E) and assessment agencies (OTA/GAO, EPTA) to assess whether the US could meet Paris Accord goals justly.", "source": "src:cw_transitions", "era": "era:graduate", "year": 2019, "efficacy": "mastery", "agency": "personal", "kolb": "AC", "strength": 3, "prov": "verified", "layer": "public", "note": "An unfinished research design, not a completed study. Worth knowing it exists: it is the most ambitious scope you have ever sketched.", "type": "Evidence"}, {"id": "ev:climate_federalism", "label": "Analysed why US climate policy stalls, through the structure of federalism", "detail": "Traced Kyoto's failed ratification, the Paris Agreement's non-binding design, the Clean Power Plan's state flexibility and the Climate Mayors' 406-city response, arguing that misinformation and abstraction have made the crisis politically unlegislatable at federal scale.", "source": "src:cw_federalism", "era": "era:graduate", "year": 2018, "efficacy": "mastery", "agency": "personal", "kolb": "AC", "strength": 3, "prov": "verified", "layer": "public", "type": "Evidence"}, {"id": "ev:eop_facilitation", "label": "Facilitated expert workshops revising a national sustainability competency framework", "detail": "Gathered structured revisions to the EOP framework: aligning it to ABET and UN SDG outcomes, embedding justice/equity/diversity/inclusion, sequencing learning outcomes by causal dependency, and collapsing overlapping outcomes by Bloom's taxonomy.", "source": "src:eop_deck", "year": 2021, "efficacy": "mastery", "agency": "collective", "kolb": "AE", "strength": 3, "prov": "verified", "layer": "public", "type": "Evidence"}, {"id": "claim:adaptive_expertise_authority", "type": "Claim", "layer": "public", "label": "I have a decade-long, published research programme on how people develop the ability to handle problems they have never seen.", "best_for": ["resume", "cover_letter", "bio", "pitch"], "prov": "verified", "note": "Strongest claim in the graph and now fully public. Five supports.", "n_supports": 5, "support_strength": 4.6, "era_span": 1, "efficacy_mix": ["mastery"], "flag": "NARROW: all evidence from one era"}, {"id": "claim:energy_transition_bridge", "type": "Claim", "layer": "public", "label": "I hold both a formal energy systems credential and the research background to understand how working engineers actually retrain.", "best_for": ["cover_letter", "pitch", "bio"], "prov": "inferred", "note": "The claim your own author bio is reaching for. Nothing else in the record asserts it yet, and no employer would infer it unaided.", "n_supports": 4, "support_strength": 4.75, "era_span": 3, "efficacy_mix": ["mastery", "physiological"], "flag": "OK"}, {"id": "claim:designs_for_self_direction", "type": "Claim", "layer": "public", "label": "I design environments that make people self-directed rather than delivering content to them.", "best_for": ["resume", "cover_letter", "pitch"], "prov": "inferred", "n_supports": 3, "support_strength": 4.67, "era_span": 1, "efficacy_mix": ["mastery"], "flag": "NARROW: all evidence from one era"}, {"id": "claim:rigorous_qual", "type": "Claim", "layer": "public", "label": "I can run a rigorous qualitative study end to end: design, protocol, fieldwork, coding, theory.", "best_for": ["resume", "cover_letter"], "prov": "verified", "n_supports": 4, "support_strength": 4.25, "era_span": 1, "efficacy_mix": ["mastery"], "flag": "NARROW: all evidence from one era"}, {"id": "claim:others_invest", "type": "Claim", "layer": "public", "label": "People who have worked with me invest their own time in my work years after the fact.", "best_for": ["cover_letter", "bio"], "prov": "inferred", "note": "Only claim in the graph resting on attestation rather than your own account. Handle it carefully; it is also the hardest kind to manufacture.", "n_supports": 2, "support_strength": 4.5, "era_span": 1, "efficacy_mix": ["social_persuasion", "vicarious"], "flag": "NARROW: all evidence from one era"}, {"id": "claim:builds_for_underserved", "type": "Claim", "layer": "public", "label": "I build for people that standard systems are not built for.", "best_for": ["cover_letter", "bio"], "prov": "inferred", "n_supports": 2, "support_strength": 4.0, "era_span": 1, "efficacy_mix": ["mastery"], "flag": "NARROW: all evidence from one era"}, {"id": "claim:workforce_energy_proven", "type": "Claim", "layer": "public", "label": "I have already built and run workforce retraining for energy workers in transition \u2014 it is not a direction I want, it is a thing I have done.", "best_for": ["resume", "cover_letter", "pitch", "bio"], "prov": "verified", "note": "This claim did not exist before this ingestion. It is now the best-supported claim in the graph and it spans four eras.", "n_supports": 5, "support_strength": 4.6, "era_span": 3, "efficacy_mix": ["mastery", "physiological"], "flag": "OK"}, {"id": "claim:decade_on_one_question", "type": "Claim", "layer": "public", "label": "I have been working on the same question since I was eighteen: how does a person gain the capability to change the situation they are in?", "best_for": ["bio", "pitch", "cover_letter"], "prov": "inferred", "note": "Spans five eras \u2014 the only claim in the graph that does. Philosophy coursework, a scout project, five papers, and a retraining bootcamp are the same enquiry in four vocabularies.", "n_supports": 5, "support_strength": 4.4, "era_span": 4, "efficacy_mix": ["mastery", "physiological"], "flag": "OK"}, {"id": "claim:field_to_framework", "type": "Claim", "layer": "public", "label": "I do the fieldwork and then write the framework \u2014 in the Pacific, in Kenya, in a classroom, and in print.", "best_for": ["resume", "cover_letter", "pitch"], "prov": "inferred", "n_supports": 4, "support_strength": 4.5, "era_span": 3, "efficacy_mix": ["mastery"], "flag": "OK"}, {"id": "theme:self_direction", "type": "Theme", "label": "The same question asked of children", "gloss": "The same question asked of children, then students, and now of working adults: how does a person come to direct their own learning", "prov": "inferred", "layer": "public"}, {"id": "theme:naming_gaps", "type": "Theme", "label": "A repeated move: find where the existing vocabulary fails", "gloss": "A repeated move: find where the existing vocabulary fails, then supply a word", "prov": "inferred", "layer": "public"}, {"id": "theme:ecology_not_instruction", "type": "Theme", "label": "Consistently designs the environment rather than the message", "gloss": "Consistently designs the environment rather than the message", "prov": "inferred", "layer": "public"}, {"id": "theme:two_unjoined_halves", "type": "Theme", "label": "An energy credential and a learning-science record that only his own a", "gloss": "An energy credential and a learning-science record that only his own author biography has ever connected", "prov": "inferred", "layer": "public"}], "edges": [{"source": "ev:two_ieee_first_author", "predicate": "demonstrates", "target": "skill:academic_writing", "prov": "verified"}, {"source": "ev:two_ieee_first_author", "predicate": "demonstrates", "target": "skill:qual_research", "prov": "verified"}, {"source": "ev:two_ieee_first_author", "predicate": "documented_in", "target": "src:ieee_cogdev", "prov": "verified"}, {"source": "ev:two_ieee_first_author", "predicate": "during_era", "target": "era:research", "prov": "verified"}, {"source": "ev:work_carried_to_print", "pred